{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1503439-what-three-types-of-renown-would-samsa-use","id":1503439,"title":"What three types of Renown would Samsa use","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-19T03:32:20-08:00","id":1503439,"title":"What three types of Renown would Samsa use","content":"Assume either:<br /> <br /> - the Samsa have achieved enough renown in the Wyrmish world to have Rank and Renown akin to the Yeren<br /> - the Samsa have betrayed the Wyrm, come to Gaia, and are being patronized by Cockroach<br /> <br /> What three types of Renown could you see them using?<br /> <br /> Initially I think that the Rokea Renown could work well, with a twist. The Weresharks are Gaia's tasked Survivors, and they use Valor, Harmony and Innovation. For the Samsa it could be Discretion, Harmony and Innovation.<br /> <br /> Discretion: keeping secrets, keeping yourself and the Breed (and its allies) safe, avoiding danger where possible, lost for actions like recklessness, exposing group secrets, drawing attention to yourself. Destroying Samsa who have remained in service to the Wyrm loses Discretion, though Cockroach refuses to discuss this with his children.<br /> <br /> Harmony: while survival is important, it is also important to fulfil other roles where possible; know your place, your part, and engage in it effectively. A Samsa would gain this for acts that help fulfil their given role, be that assassin, spy, guardian, explorer or so-on. Returning to Wyrmish ways loses Harmony.<br /> <br /> Innovation: Cockroach will ride out the Apocalypse, regardless of who wins; his genius and ability to adapt is the reason why. Innovation is granted for new ideas, inventions, Gifts and Rites being ported over to the Samsa, forging new alliances and so forth. Building a technofetish with the help of a Glass Walker would be a great example, while botching an attempt to ingratiate yourself with a Sept would cost it; your bright idea didn't work out. Cockroach has made it known that a Samsa who discovers a Rite or Gift that allows the Breed to willingly adopt a Swarm Form will gain 2 dots of Innovation on the spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T11:46:01-07:00","id":1506967,"title":"","content":"You said everything I would think of. I'd look at the Rokea, and emphasize the part where you adapt to the world you find yourself in. I dig discretion as a way of emphasizing what the books talk about with summoning and binding cockroach spirits, that they're very skittish and bail out of dangerous seeming circumstances easily. I'd incorporate that into the discretion renown. Something like a vampire path that just punishes you for risking your life pointlessly and rewards you for holding survival, personal or of your community, dear. <br /> <br /> Maybe it'd be worth looking at different kinds of cockroach cousins IRL to see the things that cockroaches adapt to. Like termites, earwigs, mantids, crickets and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}